    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Percentage of people who inject drugs reached with HIV prevention programs - defined package of services</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The numerator represents the clients (UIC), who received a minimum package of services during the reporting period including PWID prisoners.
The denominator is estimated number of PWIDs as 25,000 by PWID size estimation 2016 report.
The beneficiary is considered reached if he/she receives the minimum package which includes: distribution of IEC materials and/or information sessions can be conducted, health products (syringes with needles, alcohol napkins, condoms). For PWID prisoners the minimum package includes: distribution of IEC materials and/or information sessions can be conducted, health products (syringes with needles, alcohol napkins and access to condoms).</narrative>
    </description>
